// References: mpmath at 150 digits, printed to 40, at the double values of the parameters and arguments
// (the generator is in the PR that added this file). Where the tests need more than a few ulps, it is the
// condition number of the function, not the method:
//  * the cdf deep in its tails, exp(-t) for large t, magnifies the rounding of (x - mu)/sigma, so the
//    tolerances scale with each function's condition number;
//  * mu + sigma q cancels where the quantile is near 0 (-0.016 at xi = 1.5, p = 0.25), so the quantile's tolerance
//    scales with (|mu| + |x - mu|)/|x|;
//  * skewness and kurtosis excess pass through 0 (at xi = -0.28 and -0.15), so they are checked to an
//    absolute error, and for |xi| >= 1/4 the kurtosis is a fourth difference of lgamma(1 - k xi).

